      "instruction": "Repair SI-prefix number formatting. solve(num, suffix) returns a compact number followed by an SI prefix and the literal suffix. Prefixes are empty, K, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y with factors of 1000. Choose precision so rounding near an order boundary does not produce an extra digit (e.g. 9999 becomes 10.0K, 999999 becomes 1.00M). Preserve sign, zero, suffix and ordinary magnitudes. Inputs are finite numbers; use the existing Python numeric formatting convention.",
